      "content": "thanks. it just felt so... mechanical. and then there was this other thing—later in the clip, they were mid-sentence and their left eyelid did this tiny, rapid fluttering thing, almost like a refresh rate error on a screen? it was so fast it didn't even look like a blink. it looked like a glitch in the video itself, but the rest of the frame was perfect. does that kind of \"stuttering\" happen in natural human muscle movements, or is that something else?",
